//! Cursor-local adaptive tessellation of a procedural Fe terrain.
//!
//! Ninety-six triangular macro patches form one continuous sheet. Every patch
//! is an instance of a bounded atlas draw; its three edge demands are sampled
//! at the corresponding projected edge midpoints, so neighbours independently
//! choose exactly the same dyadic boundary density. The canonical Quilting
//! atlas supplies topology and Fe restores the requested edge permutation.
//!
//! Geometry, noise differentials, edge LoD, cursor reaction, orbit camera,
//! OKLCH heat mapping, lighting, and analytic wire coverage are all Fe. The
//! browser transports typed facts and realizes the compile-time WebGPU plan.
//! Four-sample rasterization handles silhouettes; a perspective-correct pixel
//! altitude gives every internal edge a constant-width analytic AA feather.
//!
//! `animation_clock` is the deliberately isolated clock seam. It accepts typed
//! animation-frame timestamps now, while also advancing on interaction. The
//! current resident surface host only presents frames backed by queued input,
//! so idle continuous animation awaits its planned zero-input frame contract;
//! no browser-side timer or policy is substituted here.

